								<h2 class="shadowed-gray-text tall-text title-font balanced-weave bottom-duo-spacing">Designed around everyday life</h2>
								<p class="calm-flow foundation-text">
									A room should support the routines that take place in it, not simply look appealing in a photograph. The design conversation can consider how you move through the space, what needs to be stored, where people gather and which activities happen at different times of day. These practical observations help guide choices about layout, furniture and lighting. By starting with the way a room is actually used, the design can feel more personal and relevant, while leaving room for your
									preferences and the character of the home.
								</p>
